</statement>
</exercise>

<exercise>
<statement>
<p>A symmetry group has order <m>12</m>, and an object has stabilizer of size
<m>3</m>. Find the size of its orbit.</p>
</statement>
</exercise>

<exercise>
<statement>
<p>How many binary colorings of four labeled positions exist before
symmetry is considered?</p>
</statement>
</exercise>

<exercise>
<statement>
<p>Compute</p>

<p>
<md>[4]_q.</md>
</p>
</statement>
</exercise>

<exercise>
<statement>
<p>Compute</p>

<p>
<md>[3]_q!.</md>
</p>
</statement>
</exercise>

<exercise>
<statement>
<p>Find</p>

<p>
<md>\begin{bmatrix}
3\\
1
\end{bmatrix}_q.</md>
</p>
</statement>
</exercise>

<exercise>
<statement>
<p>Draw the Young diagram of</p>

<p>
<md>\lambda=(5,3,1).</md>
</p>
</statement>
</exercise>

<exercise>
<statement>
<p>Use Burnside's lemma to count binary necklaces of length <m>3</m>.</p>
</statement>
</exercise>

<exercise>
<statement>
<p>Use Burnside's lemma to count binary necklaces of length <m>5</m>.</p>
</statement>
</exercise>

<exercise>
<statement>
<p>Count colorings of the vertices of a square using two colors up to
rotation.</p>
</statement>
</exercise>

<exercise>
<statement>
<p>Repeat the previous problem when reflections are also considered
equivalent.</p>
</statement>
</exercise>

<exercise>
<statement>
<p>Find the cycle index of <m>C_3</m> acting on three positions.</p>
</statement>
</exercise>

<exercise>
<statement>
<p>Use that cycle index to count colorings with <m>q</m> colors.</p>
</statement>
</exercise>

<exercise>
<statement>
<p>Show that a permutation with <m>c</m> cycles fixes exactly <m>q^c</m>
colorings of its positions using <m>q</m> colors.</p>
</statement>
</exercise>

<exercise>
<statement>
<p>Compute</p>

<p>
<md>\begin{bmatrix}
4\\
2
\end{bmatrix}_q.</md>
</p>
</statement>
</exercise>

<exercise>
<statement>
<p>Evaluate</p>

<p>
<md>\begin{bmatrix}
4\\
2
\end{bmatrix}_q</md>
</p>

<p>at <m>q=1</m>.</p>
</statement>
</exercise>

<exercise>
<statement>
<p>How many one-dimensional subspaces does</p>

<p>
<md>\mathbb{F}_2^3</md>
</p>

<p>contain?</p>
</statement>
</exercise>

<exercise>
<statement>
<p>Use the hook-length formula to find the number of standard Young
tableaux of shape</p>

<p>
<md>(3,1).</md>
</p>
</statement>
</exercise>

<exercise>
<statement>
<p>Write the first three elementary symmetric polynomials in</p>

<p>
<md>x_1,x_2,x_3.</md>
</p>
</statement>
</exercise>

<exercise>
<statement>
<p>Show that</p>

<p>
<md>\prod_{i=1}^{n}(1+x_it)
=
\sum_{k=0}^{n}e_kt^k.</md>
</p>
</statement>
</exercise>

<exercise>
<statement>
<p>Prove Burnside's lemma by double counting pairs</p>

<p>
<md>(g,x)</md>
</p>

<p>with <m>g\cdot x=x</m>.</p>
</statement>
</exercise>

<exercise>
<statement>
<p>Derive the necklace formula</p>

<p>
<md>N_q(n)
=
\frac1n
\sum_{d\mid n}
\varphi(d)q^{n/d}.</md>
</p>
</statement>
</exercise>

<exercise>
<statement>
<p>Derive the cycle index of <m>C_4</m>.</p>
</statement>
